# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: Reel.
Package: Reel
Section: Video
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Components: Apps.Video.!Reel (Movable LookAt), Apps.Video.!ReelEGL (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-ffmpeg
Description: Video player for the RISC OS desktop, built on FFmpeg
 Plays MP4, MKV, WebM, AVI and more (H.264, HEVC, VP9, AV1), with
 subtitles, chapters, playlists and a mini player, and web streams.
 Uses VideoOverlay and the Pi's hardware decoders where it can.
 !ReelEGL is the same player drawing through riscos-mesa's EGL.
 Needs ARMv7 with NEON.
Build-Map: !Reel -> Apps/Video/!Reel
Build-Map: !ReelEGL -> Apps/Video/!ReelEGL
Build-Notice: Reel, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-ffmpeg/releases
 .
 Reel is under the GNU GPL version 2 or later and includes FFmpeg 5.1.10
 and other libraries, which keep their own licences. Licences follow.
Build-Copyright: !Reel/docs/Licences
Build-Copyright: !ReelEGL/docs/Licences/riscos-mesa
